  data:  # 94b3
    kind: invariant  # 94b3
    title: "results cache ignores the user's analysis-stage catalogue channels: a changed or broken frameworks.d file is not seen by a cached sketch"  # 94b3
    status: violated  # 94b3
    priority: 3  # 94b3
    parent:  # 94b3
    tags:  # 94b3
    - catalogue  # 94b3
    - cache  # 94b3
    isbefore: []  # 94b3
    duplicate_of: []  # 94b3
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 94b3
    pr_ref:  # 94b3
    description: "Found 2026-10-11 while fixing INV-nuram (broken catalogue files -> exit 2). The analysis-results cache is keyed by repo state hash, opt-in backend set, trace_deps token and analyzer identity (sketch_embeddings._get_results_cache_dir), but NOT by the content of the user's analysis-stage catalogue channels ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/frameworks.d, library_signatures.d, dataflow_patterns.d). A command that reuses a cached survey therefore never sees a channel file that was added, changed or broken after the survey was cached.\n\nRepro (live, dev + INV-nuram branch): tmp repo with app.py using flask and requirements.txt 'flask'; XDG_CACHE_HOME=$T/cache XDG_CONFIG_HOME=$T/xdg. (1) 'hypergumbo survey .' -> rc 0 (cached). (2) write 'key: [unclosed' to $T/xdg/hypergumbo/frameworks.d/flask.yaml. (3) 'hypergumbo sketch .' -> rc 0, no error (cached survey reused, broken file never read). (4) 'hypergumbo survey .' -> rc 2 'Error: could not parse framework pattern file .../frameworks.d/flask.yaml'. The same staleness applies to a SOUND edit: an in-house framework definition added to frameworks.d after a cached survey does not affect sketch/verify-claims auto-discovery until something else invalidates the cache.\n\nFix direction: fold a digest of the user channel files the analysis reads (frameworks.d, library_signatures.d, dataflow_patterns.d; in-repo tier too if opted in) into the results-cache key, the way trace_deps is folded in."  # 94b3
    fields:  # 94b3
      statement: "A cached analysis result is reused only when the user catalogue channel files the analysis reads are unchanged since it was cached."  # 94b3
      root_cause: "_get_results_cache_dir keys the cache on repo state, backend set, trace_deps and analyzer identity, not on the user's frameworks.d / library_signatures.d / dataflow_patterns.d contents."  # 94b3
