- op: discuss  # 19e8
  at: '2026-10-12T06:45:44Z'  # 19e8
  by: agent  # 19e8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 19e8
  clock: 3  # 19e8
  nonce: '19e8'  # 19e8
  message: "Fixed in 3989655c22 (fix(cache): the results-cache key carries the user files the analysis reads). Root cause: _get_results_cache_dir keyed on repo state, backends, trace_deps and analyzer identity only, so analysis-stage user channels (frameworks.d, library_signatures.d, dataflow_patterns.d) and config.toml / .hypergumbo.toml were never re-read once a survey was cached. Fix: CatalogSpec.channel_stage (analysis|command) is required for every family with a user channel; analysis-stage channel files and both config tiers are digested into -cat-<hash> / -cfg-<hash> suffixes, each absent when its files are. Live evidence on dev 3989655c22 (fresh XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_CACHE_HOME, Flask fixture): (0) no channel files: sketch exit 0, key 4c2813d0f3ca2b76; (1) valid frameworks.d/flask.yaml: exit 0, new key 4c2813d0f3ca2b76-cat-5fd39d5f79a7; (2) same file broken: exit 2, 'Error: could not parse framework pattern file .../frameworks.d/flask.yaml: while parsing a flow sequence' (before the fix this was a cache hit at exit 0); (3) file restored: exit 0, reuses -cat-5fd39d5f79a7, no new dir; (4) file removed: exit 0, reuses the bare 4c2813d0f3ca2b76 key, so users with no channel files keep their existing key; (5) broken config.toml: exit 2, 'not valid TOML — Expected ]'; (6) config removed: exit 0. Production-path test: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_results_cache_input_key.py."  # 19e8
